<title>USA: Valmont Industries Q4 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Valmont Industries Q4 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>VALLEY, Neb. 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.05   profit	 $0.51</p>
<p> Net loss		     777   profit	 7,103</p>
<p> Revs		     180,720		  140,732</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  14,194		   13,829</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q4 results include $10.1 million after-tax charge to reduce the value of the company's investment in Valmont Electric. Excluding the charge, earnings were $9.3 million or $0.66/shr in the 1996 Q4.  </p>
<p>			YEAR</p>
<p> Shr profit		$ 1.52   profit	 $1.80</p>
<p> Net profit		21,248   profit	24,759</p>
<p> Revs		     644,531		  544,642</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  14,017		   13,733</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Periods ended December 28 vs December 30.</p>
<p>1996 full-year earnings prior to the charge for reducing the company's investment in Valmont Electric were $31.3 million or $2.24/shr.</p>
<p>Full name is Valmont Industries Inc.</p>
<p>	 ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
